  "reason": "R8 and R18 closely anticipate the central design: adding Cr to a refractory BCC multicomponent alloy produces a network-distributed Cr-rich Laves phase, while Cr simultaneously contributes solid-solution strengthening and the Laves phase contributes precipitation strengthening. R6 independently supports the tendency of Cr-containing refractory BCC alloys to decompose by forming Cr-based Laves phases. Other records establish that dilute additions can raise both strength and plasticity through lattice distortion or ordered complexes, and that second-phase morphology can materially affect mechanical behavior. The records do not directly report the later paper's specific crack-deflection/plasticity-compensation mechanism or the precise 4.2 at.% Cr level in HfMoTaTiZr, but the near-identical Cr/network-Laves precedent makes the intervention and a morphology-dependent strengthening mechanism plausibly reconstructible by an expert."
